{
  "_comment": "Hand-authored setup content. NOT generated -- the importers never touch this file. Two separate things live here. `species` is a per-species profile: the Home Terrain a species brings and the second terrain it proposes as the Frontier, which the loser of the Horde roll-off places (PLAN-V1.md Phase 0a). With only three terrain types in the box and element-matching leaving each species just two legal ones, both of which it would otherwise spend on its home, the second is a second die of its own type -- Tower at home, City at the Frontier, so the two dice differ. Phase 5 adds three more types and makes that a real choice. `presets` are named forces, kept because a test that wants a particular die on the board has to be able to say so, and because the golden corpus needs forces that never change. The two `_starter` lists are the 30-health ones the alpha shipped with; the two `_bestiary` lists are 35 health and hold one of every monster and every large die of their species, which is the widest SAI coverage a legal force can reach. The ten monster fixtures are one per monster die in the data -- six copies of that one monster, split 3/2/1 across home, Frontier and the enemy home. They exist so a rule about a monster face can be watched happening: six of one die against six of another is a game made of nothing but the two faces under test, where a bestiary buries the interesting die among nineteen others that may never roll. Six is what the setup cap allows -- 24 health, so no army may exceed 12, which is exactly the three at home. All ten are 24 health, so any two of them pair, mirrors included; none of them pairs with a starter (30) or a bestiary (35). An ordinary game rolls its forces from the seed instead.",
